{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098952-how-do-you-justify-giving-a-satyr-wings","id":1098952,"title":"How do you justify giving a Satyr wings?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-31T18:27:17-07:00","id":1098952,"title":"How do you justify giving a Satyr wings?","content":"I love the Supernatural Merits and Flaws, but I sense a problem. Wings were never a part of the myth of Satyrs or Trolls, so how can I justify giving them this merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T18:32:12-07:00","id":1098957,"title":"","content":"Maybe the satyr has some griffon in his lineage? <br /> Maybe the satyr drank a magic potion while in the Far Dreaming?<br /> Maybe the troll is Greek, and is descended from the Furies?<br /> Maybe the troll's wings are made of ice and're an unusually powerful side-effect of learning Kryos?<br /> <br /> Note:<br /> As an aside, I had a Leanhaun sidhe Big Bad is a CtD game I ran <i>yeeeeeeaaars</i> ago, and he had wings. This Leanhaun duke's wings were the result of a chimerical hawk of great power having its heart ritually eaten at Samhain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 05-31-2017, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T18:34:01-07:00","id":1098958,"title":"","content":"Cupid had them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T19:01:45-07:00","id":1098972,"title":"","content":"If blessings from a dragon can give the fae the power of dragons in the form of dragon's ire, why not some draconic lookin wings? Perhaps even make something plot hook-ish out of it, some event occurred in the cycle of their incarnations involving the gifting of said power, and now the dragon is looking for a favour repay (or revenge if they somehow took it, or what have you). There's lots of ways to spin that kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T20:06:17-07:00","id":1099000,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098952-how-do-you-justify-giving-a-satyr-wings?p=1098972#post1098972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If blessings from a dragon can give the fae the power of dragons in the form of dragon's ire, why not some draconic lookin wings? Perhaps even make something plot hook-ish out of it, some event occurred in the cycle of their incarnations involving the gifting of said power, and now the dragon is looking for a favour repay (or revenge if they somehow took it, or what have you). There's lots of ways to spin that kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Come to think of it. Goat legs. Horns. Passion and <i>sin</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Bat wings</b> are often assosiated with <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Succubus\" target=\"_blank\">Succubi and Incubi</a> in modern depictions. Satyrs looks were incorpotated into medieval demons, such as Slavic <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bies\" target=\"_blank\">Bies</a>, <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chort\" target=\"_blank\">Chort</a> and generally European <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil\" target=\"_blank\">Devil</a>. Considering that there's no canon in folklore, having bat wings isn't too far fetched.<br /> <br /> Trolls are too often are a victim of memetic mutation nowadays and might look differently. They also might have bat or scaly wings or even wings made out of pure Eldritch Prime, born due to their ties to Nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-31-2017, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T22:18:26-07:00","id":1099022,"title":"","content":"Give them a Redbull.<br /> <br /> More seriously there's alot of things that were &quot;never a part of myth&quot; that are a part of changeling(and vice versa) giving someone wings is not a huge issue if it was it would say something like(Pooka only)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:14:34-07:00","id":1099054,"title":"","content":"Sometimes it's not part of the rules but goes versus player's/GM's guts (and sometimes ignorance), so having few more arguments &quot;for&quot; never hurts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:23:55-07:00","id":1099059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098952-how-do-you-justify-giving-a-satyr-wings?p=1099054#post1099054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes it's not part of the rules but goes versus player's/GM's guts (and sometimes ignorance), so having few more arguments &quot;for&quot; never hurts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The WIngs Merit got into the books because it looked really cool to draw Sidhe with wings. There's no real mythic connection aside from &quot;that looks cool&quot;. You can get a pretty good &quot;Gargoyle&quot; look with Trolls they even match up much of the Disney Gargoyle vibe(outside the stone part). Similarly you get a pretty good demon look with Satyr+Wings. One could also point out the whole wings as symbolic for divine messenger thing that was developed into the angel visual that one could easily backgate onto various Kiths. Or you have dragonblood, or you bargained with something.. <br /> <br /> <br /> Or as always Steampunk cyberware installed by a knocker! Knockers give everyone wings(Caution don't fly too close to the sun!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T02:07:01-07:00","id":1099081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098952-how-do-you-justify-giving-a-satyr-wings?p=1099059#post1099059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The WIngs Merit got into the books because it looked really cool to draw Sidhe with wings. There's no real mythic connection aside from &quot;that looks cool&quot;. You can get a pretty good &quot;Gargoyle&quot; look with Trolls they even match up much of the Disney Gargoyle vibe(outside the stone part). Similarly you get a pretty good demon look with Satyr+Wings. One could also point out the whole wings as symbolic for divine messenger thing that was developed into the angel visual that one could easily backgate onto various Kiths. Or you have dragonblood, or you bargained with something..<br /> <br /> <br /> Or as always Steampunk cyberware installed by a knocker! Knockers give everyone wings(Caution don't fly too close to the sun!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't argue. I completely agree that it's added because of winged fairies trope and sheer Rule of Cool. That said:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/images/ic/976x549/p03m89yk.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/25/Sir_Joseph_Noel_Paton_-_The_Quarrel_of_Oberon_and_Titania_-_Google_Art_Project_2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Colloquially speaking, Elves with wings, specifically elves, is a given. And many other kinds of fair folk.<br /> <br /> But winged Troll/Orge, while not impossible, is a bit of a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-01-2017, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T06:24:11-07:00","id":1099131,"title":"","content":"I had a player make a deal with a Demon (as in, Demon the Fallen type). He happened to have wings as part of his form, and the deal gave the player's satyr the merit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T07:21:32-07:00","id":1099144,"title":"","content":"Justifying a Satyr with wings is rather easy as said earlier, there are plenty of horned and goatlegged being with wings like succubi/incubi and traditional demonic look in general including mediaval depictions of the Devil itself. Pooka are easy as there are plenty of animals/insects with wings. <br /> Sidhe as show'n above are rather easy to justify as well, beautiful fey beings, angels and many more beside are often depicted with wings. Unseelie, and Balor, Sidhe specifically could also have more &quot;monstrous&quot; wings like batwings Etc. While Dougal Sidhe, especially after how their House works in C20' would soar on mechanical clocwork wings.<br /> Trolls and Redcaps fit the bill as far as gargoyles go, as both are know for occasionally manifesting stony skin aswell.<br /> Sluagh could glide silently through the air on wings of shadow, spider silk or flywings.<br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> Even the Mer could be justified by giving them wing like fins of flyingfishes.<br /> <br /> Pretty much the only Kith I find difficult to justify having wings are the Selkie though that is entirely due to my own failings as I dont find seals to be that inspiring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":".  Typos 06-01-2017, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T07:41:38-07:00","id":1099148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098952-how-do-you-justify-giving-a-satyr-wings?p=1099144#post1099144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trolls and Redcaps fit the bill as far as gargoyles go, as both are know for occasionally manifesting stony skin aswell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, Gargoyles... Missed that in previous comments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098952-how-do-you-justify-giving-a-satyr-wings?p=1099144#post1099144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much the only Kith I find difficult to justify having wings are the Selkie though that is entirely due to my own failings as I<br /> dont find seals to be that inspiring.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AtlantisIsBoring\" target=\"_blank\">Atlantis Is Boring</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T09:29:21-07:00","id":1099185,"title":"","content":"Selkies with wings? Easy: a chimerical bird sleeps on the selkie's back and, when awoken, can carry the selkie places the selkie asks to go to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T10:35:27-07:00","id":1099212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098952-how-do-you-justify-giving-a-satyr-wings?p=1099022#post1099022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give them a Redbull.</div> </div> </div> </div>I opened this thread to see if someone had posted this. Thank you for not letting me down!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:11:08-07:00","id":1099257,"title":"","content":"In answer to the original question: A gift from the Olympian gods for some service performed in this or in some past incarnation.<br /> <br /> In the case of Trolls, if it was a female, a riff on Freya's cloak of falcon feathers, especially if she's taken up some sort of role of modern day valkyrie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T13:20:52-07:00","id":1099259,"title":"","content":"QUOTE=Firkraag;n1099081]<br /> Oh, I don't argue. I completely agree that it's added because of winged fairies trope and sheer Rule of Cool. That said:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/images/ic/976x549/p03m89yk.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/25/Sir_Joseph_Noel_Paton_-_The_Quarrel_of_Oberon_and_Titania_-_Google_Art_Project_2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Colloquially speaking, Elves with wings, specifically elves, is a given. And many other kinds of fair folk.<br /> <br /> But winged Troll/Orge, while not impossible, is a bit of a stretch.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm just going to point out the batwinged Faun on the first image...<br /> <br /> <br /> And do I really need to get out the countless images of Gargoyles?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urabyfirst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098952-how-do-you-justify-giving-a-satyr-wings?p=1099131#post1099131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a player make a deal with a Demon (as in, Demon the Fallen type). He happened to have wings as part of his form, and the deal gave the player's satyr the merit</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did he win them in a Fiddling contest? DID HE?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T14:10:23-07:00","id":1099282,"title":"","content":"IIRC, in the Merits &amp; Flaws section of the original Changeling Players Guide, it had a picture of a female Redcap with succubus-style bat wings on or near the wings merit write up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T14:11:13-07:00","id":1099283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1098952-how-do-you-justify-giving-a-satyr-wings?p=1099259#post1099259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did he win them in a Fiddling contest? DID HE?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know perfectly well that the Rule of Awesome dictates that he did. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\